{"chunk_id": "ea2a2e336286", "text": "These pages recount the tragic chain of events leading from Daksha\u2019s insult to Shiva to the cosmic consequences that follow. Sati, distressed by her father\u2019s hostility, first doubts Shiva\u2019s reverence for Rama and tests the prince by assuming Sita\u2019s form. Rama reveals his universal form (Vishvarupa), humbling Sati and deepening the moral weight of her disobedience to Shiva. Later, ignoring Shiva\u2019s warning, she attends Daksha\u2019s grand sacrifice where her father publicly insults Shiva. Unable to endure the dishonor and remorseful for her earlier actions, Sati meditates on Shiva and immolates herself in the sacrificial fire. Her death triggers divine retribution: Shiva creates the fierce warrior Virabhadra and the goddess Bhadra Kali to destroy Daksha\u2019s yajna. The episode highlights devotion, cosmic justice, and the devastating consequences of pride and disrespect toward the divine.\nSati tests Rama, is rebuked, later humiliated by Daksha and immolates herself at his sacrifice, prompting Shiva to create Virabhadra to destroy the yajna.\nThemes: divine pride and insult, devotion and doubt, self\u2011immolation of Sati, cosmic revelation, divine vengeance", "vector": [-0.006694817915558815, -0.006753889843821526, -0.008545738644897938, 0.003626359859481454, -0.017288383096456528, 0.009038004092872143, -0.045052189379930496, 0.0016966769471764565, -0.014019737020134926, -0.024416396394371986, 0.019835039973258972, 0.018942397087812424, 0.017012713477015495, 0.010547620244324207, 0.001137954997830093, 0.0061894250102341175, 0.04833396151661873, -0.0014357758918777108, 0.04268931224942207, -0.02152843400835991, 0.006872033700346947, -0.003833111608400941, 0.001737699145451188, 0.03420920670032501, -0.023970074951648712, 0.013008950278162956, 0.014846744015812874, -0.03827860578894615, 0.014557947404682636, -0.002697617979720235, -0.02477082796394825, -0.02471831813454628, -0.00819787010550499, -0.0142297